{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine","id":1548281,"title":"Running the Free States - 2 - Germaine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-06T17:29:26-08:00","id":1548281,"title":"Running the Free States - 2 - Germaine","content":"Germaine was the only Anarch on the original Red List as revealed by the Kindred\u2019s Most Wanted sourcebook. As such, he should be a figure just as well known as Jeremy MacNeil, Salvador Garcia, and Smiling Jack IMO. He\u2019s not as he wasn\u2019t really mentioned or developed outside that sourcebook. So I am going to correct that in this chronicle. I'm going to have him show up and interact with the PCs at some point. If you haven't read that sourcebook, there's going to be spoilers here.<br /> <br /> As written, Germaine is one of the childer of Critias so he has quite potent blood. He was an earlier supporter of the French Revolution, but mostly as a mortal and ghoul. He was not embraced until quite late, hates his sire (whose name he does not know), and was used as a scapegoat by Toreador vampires (Countess D\u2019Adhemar and her sire, Madame Guil).<br /> <br /> Both of them also supported the French Revolution for their own reasons, but had to hide it because they were effectively traitors to their own clan who dominated Paris and France. They basically blamed Germaine for everything, and when the Camarilla created the Red List, Madame Guil put his name on it. She doesn\u2019t really hunt after him, but her childe the Countess does because Germaine could reveal her personal secrets and therefore get her killed.<br /> <br /> It's mentioned explicitly that Geramine does not &quot;deserve&quot; to be on the Red List. He's there out of pure spite. However, simply that is on it means a lot of Kindred, particularly anarchs, must think he's some tremendous badass that has done something even more outstanding than even MacNeil, Salvador, or Smiling Jack. I imagine there's some Chuck Norris style jokes told about him.<br /> <br /> Germaine actually left Paris very early for North America because he wants to kill his sire whom he blames for his troubles. Critias seems to find this funny because he actually helps him secretly to escape the Red List hunters.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re not given any escapades of Germaine. So I must invent various actions and events that he's done. We just know he helps the anarchs, doesn\u2019t mention his name, and is always on the move. Always trying to find his sire (whose face he remembers). He must use various aliases as he tells no one his real name, but probably gets identified as Germain after he leaves. That has built up his legend. He is very much a loner and does not make friends.<br /> <br /> = =<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council\">Part 1 - the Anarch Council</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance\">Part 3 - Governance</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs\">Part 4 - Canon Characters &amp; Gangs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites\">Part 5 - Setites</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla\">Part 6 - the Camarilla</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club\">Part 7 - San Francisco</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat\">Part 8 - Sabbat</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements\">Part 9 - Crossovers</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552818-running-the-free-states-10-the-oddball-stuff\">Part 10 - Oddballs</a>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  adding links 08-01-2025, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T17:35:58-08:00","id":1548282,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m inclined to use him as a kind of wandering Batman/Robin Hood/Scarlet Pimpernel of the Anarchs. He tends to show up in a Camarilla city and helps out Anarchs in trouble before moving on again. He\u2019s a lot like Smiling Jack except he tends to fix problems instead of fucking things up, and doesn\u2019t embrace childer of his own.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking Germaine does not reside in Los Angeles, but probably frequently visits there for some R&amp;D. He ignores MacNeil and the Anarch Council because he just does his own thing. He still keeps his identity secret because the Trophy Clan benefits are a lot, and would attract a lot of Kindred (even among the anarchs) to betray him if they knew about him. That is also why he moves around a lot. I imagine everyone on the Anarch Council has figured out who he is, but keeps his secret. His main concerns are survival and trying to destroy his sire.<br /> <br /> I wonder if he should visit Louis Fortier when he is in town as both are French. It'd probably be nice to speak in one's native language from time to time. The Vignes family in LABN has dots in Linguistics, and as older upper crust Americans from the 19th century probably know French so I was already thinking there was some &quot;French Roundtable&quot; where French speakers would meet in Louis's mansion for social entertainment, and it would be a good place for Germaine to occasionally visit when he's in town.<br /> <br /> In terms of things for the actual PCs, I see him as someone the PCs might run into time to time, perhaps even have him as someone who helped them during their backstory, or have him appear when needed to get them out of one bad jam. Then slowly reveal clues that this guy they know happens to be on the Red List.<br /> <br /> So I intend for this to be a mystery that the PCs can discover on their own at some point. I am also thinking about how to introduce Countess D'Adhemar in this as she's the one Kindred most likely to want to hunt Germaine, and if I use him I pretty much need to introduce her too at some point. Otherwise what is the point? If I have a Red List character show up, I need to involve the Red List as a topic at some point.<br /> <br /> If you have any ideas on stories that I - as the ST - could tell about him, feel free to put them here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T13:39:38-08:00","id":1548304,"title":"","content":"Having done some research on <i>Monsieur</i> (Pardonnez-moi, <i>Citoyen</i>) Germaine, I\u2019ve done my best to puzzle out a rough timeline for the fellow, despite one or two apparent contradictions:-<br /> <br /> - My best guess is that he\u2019d have been born in the early to mid 1760s (Given that he was made a ghoul at some point not long before the French Revolution and would have stopped aging at that point, even before becoming a vampire in AD 1792).<br /> <br /> - We know he was old enough to have political opinions in 1776 (and extremely passionate ones) so one might assume he was a teenager (and not an especially young one).<br /> <br /> - He\u2019s noted to have joined a \u2018Girondist cell\u2019 prior to the Revolution, but this is an anachronism, since the Girondists themselves only received the nickname in 1792 and were apparently not in existence as an organised body prior to the Estates General summoned by King Louis just before the French Revolution: one assumes that while Germaine shared their \u2018Romantic Republicanism\u2019 he wasn\u2019t associated with the Girondists until rather later (Possibly because he either joined the movement during his period as a Double Agent or just because he was actually from the Gironde, like many of that faction\u2019s founding members).<br /> <br /> - I\u2019m further assuming that, while not an Aristocrat himself, he was from the sort of bourgeoise family with an eye to either acquiring a title or \u2018marrying up\u2019 and would have been given a solid grounding in how to enter polite society (Not unlike a number of the French Revolutionary leadership).<br /> <br /> - He\u2019s noted to have been brought before Critias and made his ghoul (Along with the rest of his \u2018Girondist Cell\u2019) before the French Revolution (Critias apparently keeping residence in a small Swiss village): given he seems<br /> to have been recruited specifically to work his way into the confidences of the Countess d\u2019Adhemar (Sired 1789) it seems<br /> likely that this occurred in the late 1780s.<br /> <br /> - Note that at this time the Countess d\u2019Adhemar\u2019s<br /> sire, the future Madame Guil, was one of the most dangerous Anarchs (and ferocious diablerists) in France: it seems highly likely she made the Countess a vampire in order to have an \u2018in\u2019 to the French court (possibly to the outer layers of the Camarilla as well), only for Critias of the Brujah to detect this gambit and take measures intended to plant his own agent close to the Countess (Presumably to make certain that the French Revolution would be the \u2018right\u2019 sort of Revolution and given himself the exact same \u2018in\u2019 with Royal circles).<br /> <br /> My guess is that the future Madame Guil (At this point known as Gilles and possibly going around in drag, given that \u2018Gilles\u2019 is a masculine Christian name) attracted Critias\u2019 attention by virtue of being the Childe of Philippe Vollgirre (A Toreador of the 5th Generation who was old by 1579 and the epitome<br /> of a feudal tyrant: it\u2019s easy to imagine him as an old enemy of Critias as a result, possibly even as far back as the days when Marseilles was a Hellenistic port, given \u2018Phillipe\u2019 is a name with Greek origins).<br /> <br /> I\u2019d bet cash money Critias recruited Germaine in order to acquire a true blue Revolutionary who actually liked (or at least knew how to get along with) the ladies, a quality I expect to have been in short supply amongst Critias\u2019 circle.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Incidentally, one expects that the Countess may have been a protege of the future Madame Guil (possibly her ghoul as well) prior to her Embrace: in fact I would guess that she insinuated herself into court circles as a mortal and was embraced only when sufficiently deep for her \u2018disappearance\u2019 to attract unwonted attention.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Anyway, for at least a couple of years (Possibly 1789-1792) Germaine (Possibly as \u2018Count Germaine\u2019, though whether in the character of a Swiss or a Frenchman) used d\u2019Adhemar to work his way into French Court circles, facilitate the Revolution and make life more difficult for the Toreador, acting as Critias double agent.<br /> <br /> - At some point after the Revolution he was rumbled, went on the run and ran into Critias, who made him a vampire in 1792 and taught him the use of his new powers before the Methuselah went his own way (Incidentally, this timeline of events very probably kills my pet theory that Critias was in Philadelphia at the time the US constitution was being drafted stone-dead): Germaine proceeded to thoroughly enjoy Revolutionary France, not least by hunting down and feeding on counter-revolutionary elements.<br /> <br /> - This period of Revolutionary bliss seems to have lasted into 1793, at which point the Countess (with the help of some agents) ambushed him in a park and attempted to express her displeasure at his misuse of her: Germaine escaped, but was obliged to flee to the New World, one jump ahead of the Toreador (Apparently in search of his sire, whom he suspected - fairly or unfairly - of having played some role in the ambush).<br /> <br /> - Note that the newly-dubbed Madame Guil makes her debut with the Camarilla after the Revolution (Apparently helping the French Toreador help clean up the mess made of their assets) and begins the process of acquiring the base of support that will allow her to eventually become Justicar (My presumption is that she was not yet a Justicar at the time her second child\u2019s was sired in 1802, but that she had been firmly accepted by the Camarilla before this point).<br /> <br /> What role, if any, the Countess d\u2019Adhemar played<br /> in this process remains unknown (It was presumably only after Madame Guil became Justicar for Clan Toreador that she was able to place Germaine\u2019s name on the Red List, at a guess sometime towards the middle of the 19th century).<br /> <br /> <br /> - After this dates become few, but we know that Germaine travelled across the United States and learned a fine contempt for the Camarilla, involved himself with the Anarchs and was courted by the Sabbat (All of which may well have helped to place him on the Red List).<br /> <br /> He also continued to be manipulated against Madame Guil by Critias (Whether knowingly or unknowingly).<br /> <br /> <br /> - We know that at some point he only narrowly escaped destruction by the Justicar Petrodon in Seattle (Probably after the Justicar escalates his efforts against the Anarchs in 1984 and certainly before the latter\u2019s Final Death in 1997), going on the run towards the East Coast (Suggesting he\u2019d somehow burned his bridges to the Anarch Free States or that, as a badly-mauled fugitive, he needed to make a move his opponents would not reasonably predict), apparently arriving in Chicago at some point in the late 1990s and hooking up with Damien to teach the local Anarchs where they came from and where they ought to be heading. <br /> <br /> <br /> - Incidentally, Madame Guil, the Justicar who placed Germaine on the Red List, appears to have gone rogue from the Camarilla herself (Having hooked up with Luc, an old flame from her Anarch days now associated with the Sabbat - as a Templar), an old flame having burned out any commitment to the Ivory Tower (Whether Luc reciprocated by dumping the Black Hand or the ex-Justicar was planning to turn Sabbat remains unknown), only to be destroyed at some<br /> point before 2012.<br /> <br /> Whether or not Germaine himself played any role in this sequence of events, he must have been mightily tempted to fly in and dance on her ashes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T14:37:00-08:00","id":1548307,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this is stating the obvious to the readers, but I wanted to make the facts on which I intended to build some suppositions perfectly clear.<br /> <br /> For the record, those suppositions are:-<br /> <br /> - That Germaine very consciously adopted his nom de<br /> plume from the late Comte de Saint-Germain, who may or<br /> may not have been a previous associate of Critias or even a member of his circle.<br /> <br /> - That Germaine may well have arrived in the Western Hemisphere at Saint-Domingue, not the United States and played a role in the war with the British and Spanish there, before proceeding to the United States (Possibly after the British were finally convinced to leave in 1797).<br /> <br /> (Alternatively, he may have played some role in the Whisky Rebellion of New England as it reached it\u2019s climax in 1794).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Which would mean that Germaine, loudest and proudest of French Revolutionaries, would have arrived in the US of A just in time to fall foul of the Alien &amp; Sedition Acts of 1798, which took a rather dim view of such rhetoric.<br /> <br /> If he arrived in the United States a bit earlier in the Adams Administration, one might suggest that he played a key role in ticking off Kindred Elders to the point where they lent their backing to the Acts.<br /> <br /> <br /> - I\u2019m assuming that, ousted from the US proper and deeply disillusioned by Napoleon\u2019s betrayal of Haiti and the Revolution, Germaineah have lay quiet for a time (Possibly in what shortly thereafter became the Louisiana Purchase), only to take up arms against Great Britain in the War of 1812 (Napoleon or no Napol\u00e9on, a chance to hit back against the \u2018English\u2019 on behalf of the United States would likely cheer this vampire up).<br /> <br /> Note that if the Camarilla sided with the British, as seems plausible, this may have been a key precondition for Germaine\u2019s place on the Red List (Coupled with his activities in France and Haiti, not to mention Madame Guil\u2019s<br /> steady ascent of the Ivory Tower).<br /> <br /> <br /> - One further suspects that Germaine would have been enthusiastic in his support for the Upper and Lower Canada Rebellions of 1837-1838 (Possibly the Patriot War which took place toward the end of that period) only to be richly disappointed by the British holding on to the Canadas, albeit with some degree of reform.<br /> <br /> <br /> - If his hopes of the New World had been consistently disappointed, he may have spent time exploring the North American interior as a sort of nocturnal Voyageur, slowly being drawn back to European-American civilisation by the impending Crisis of the US Civil War, only to find his attention being drawn still further south by the Old World meddling in the new.<br /> <br /> (Alternatively, he could have tried to return to Europe, inspired by the \u2018Year of Revolutions\u2019, but been thwarted by the wave of reaction and counter-Revolution across the continent).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Assuming that Germaine WAS severely disappointed by \u2018Napoleon the Great\u2019, it\u2019s quite possible that he played some role in Mexican resistance to the \u2018Second Mexican Empire\u2019 (As backed by Napoleon III) between 1864-1869.<br /> <br /> It may well be at this time that he made a closer acquaintance of the Sabbat: My suggestion is that he could have been approached (At this time or earlier) by the former Anarch \u2018Luc\u2019 (A Frenchman active as an Anarch not long prior to the French Revolution to boot), a contact which (If he had not already been placed on the Red List) might well have been enough to earn him that \u2018honour\u2019.<br /> <br /> <br /> - NOTE: If the Countess d\u2019Adhemar were part of the French efforts against the Mexican Republic (A useful cloak for efforts by the Camarilla to dislodge the Sabbat from Mexico, the city and the nation), then it seems likely she and her <i>bete noir</i> would clash.<br /> <br /> If she, like her brood mate, were an Archon by this point, her injury or destruction would be another point in the case for Germaine being put on the Red List (and a feather in Germaine\u2019s cap, so far as the Anarch\u2019s were concerned).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Incidentally, while Germaine only \u2018officially\u2019 reaches Chicago in the late 1990s, it\u2019s quite possible that he came close to Critias on one or more previous occasions (Especially in his efforts against British North America) only to bounce off a far more powerful vampire who was also his sire.<br /> <br /> <br /> - It seems possible that Germaine could have been in New England when Jeremy MacNeil was ousted (In fact the two of them may have been \u2018tidied out\u2019 at the same time, being equally associated with the Anarch tendency).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Assuming a pattern of operations against British interests, it\u2019s possible that Germaine was recruited by his clan mate Roman Pendragon for the effort to make Great Britain a Brujah stronghold during the absence of Mithras (An effort brought to a speedy end after the return of the Prince in the mid-1880s).<br /> <br /> <br /> - It\u2019s also possible that Germaine could have come back to Europe during the establishment of the Third Republic following the Franco-Prussian War: how long before the French Toreador or other interested parties tracked him down I leave to your imagination.<br /> <br /> - It\u2019s a racing certainty that if Germaine played no part in the establishment of the First Anarch Free State, he\u2019d have showed up in LA as swiftly as Lenin arrived in Petrograd after the Russian Revolution (Though probably not with the exact same impact), making LA his \u2018home away from home\u2019 from 1944 (Though whether he\u2019s the sort to make lasting friendships in any area is an interesting question).<br /> <br /> - I like the idea that his brush with Petrodon in Seattle was closely associated with the latter\u2019s escalation of operations against the Anarchs in 1984 (Presumably Seattle had been Germaine\u2019s focus for some little time).<br /> <br /> - Finally, I really like the idea that Germaine (Whether directly or indirectly) played a role in the sequence of events that pulled Madame Guil out of the Camarilla: whether he did so as a deliberate gambit or because he\u2019d given Luc information that allowed the latter to identify his old paramour is an interesting question,<br /> <br /> <br /> - Oh, and it amuses me to imagine Germaine and Smiling Jack as an effective combination but a distinctly Odd Couple: something of a case study in the difference between a professional Revolutionary and a part-time Anarchist, part-time terrorist (With Germaine the organised fanatic and secret agent, Smiling Jack the disorganised rabble-rouser and jackhammer of social structures).<br /> <br /> The two of them don\u2019t like each other AT ALL, but they\u2019ve done more damage to the Authorities than to each other.<br /> <br /> Even if Germaine is the only being on Earth to refer to Jack as \u201cEnglish Jack\u201d (Which the latter accepts in the spirit it was offered).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T14:41:34-08:00","id":1548308,"title":"","content":"P.S. I can definitely see Germaine as a sort of inverted Scarlet Pimpernel with elements of Comrade Karla from the novels of Mr John Le Carre (I tend to see him as someone who operates more as a subversive and covert operative than as any sort of vigilante or outlaw hero: a very sober, professional sort of Revolutionary in the Bolshevik spirit).<br /> <br /> Mostly works undercover right up until the Revolution comes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T14:42:51-08:00","id":1548309,"title":"","content":"I wonder if he sometimes borrows alter egos from the Comte de Saint Germaine? (Or if, as one of his few jokes, he adopts the names of Catholic Saints, especially those with aristocratic ancestry, for his cover identities).<br /> <br /> Completely forgot to add: I would also bet cash money that Smiling Jack is somehow connected to Germaine\u2019s acquisition of apparently-extensive tattoos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T18:51:06-08:00","id":1548317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548307#post1548307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Assuming that Germaine WAS severely disappointed by \u2018Napoleon the Great\u2019, it\u2019s quite possible that he played some role in Mexican resistance to the \u2018Second Mexican Empire\u2019 (As backed by Napoleon III) between 1864-1869.<br /> <br /> It may well be at this time that he made a closer acquaintance of the Sabbat:</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like this idea a lot. It broadens his experience in North America by quite a bit as Mexico is not often considered by Americans in our history of the continent. Many players know the general canon history of the US and Canada in the game, but much less about the Camarilla and Sabbat conflicts in Mexico. Simply dropping, &quot;I was in Mexico at the time,&quot; by Germaine would add a lot of mystery to him. The French invasion of Mexico and Benito Juarez's struggle against it is a perfect drama for struggle between the Anarchs, Camarilla, and Sabbat. And it seems very neglected part of the setting.<br /> <br /> It would also help explain that he does have some Sabbat contacts and occasionally does work with them, but is wary enough to not be snared by them. Involvement with the Sabbat in 1860s would put him in contact with the sect when it was much more decentralized and not as insane as it would become after 1933 with the ending of the second civil war and establishment of the revised Code of Milan. So safer than it would be with the current Sabbat. His contacts are probably more with the Loyalist faction and Cainites like Dominique Touraine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548307#post1548307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if Germaine is the only being on Earth to refer to Jack as \u201cEnglish Jack\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I will definitely be using this. I imagine the two have a grudging respect like rival pirate captains during the Golden Age of Piracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548307#post1548307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if he sometimes borrows alter egos from the Comte de Saint Germaine?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of his aliases is &quot;Count Germaine&quot;. I assume its because neonates who don't know any better confuse him with the Comte de Saint Germaine. Germaine himself would never use such an obvious alias, but it makes sense that people who figured out who he is might incorrectly call him Count Germaine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T09:44:31-08:00","id":1548367,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I\u2019m glad that some of this proved useful - incidentally, the Comte de Saint-Germaine himself was so prone to use aliases that Wikipedia lists at least half a dozen of them, so it occurred to me that if \u2018Germaine\u2019 was willing to use one of the old mystery\u2019s names as an alias, why but more than one of them? (At least prior to the creation of the Internet: it\u2019s much harder to enjoy little historic in-jokes since the invention of the Search Engine).<br /> <br /> Speaking of aliases and of urban legends that have cropped up around Germaine over his career, I\u2019d bet cash money that at least one rumour suggests that he was the original COUNT OF MONTE CRISTO - whether this was Smiling Jack trying to get Germaine targeted by moochers looking for a little of that \u2018hidden treasure\u2019 of someone seeing the vague parallels between two French characters prone to fake membership of the Aristocracy for their own ingenious ends I leave to your imagination.<br /> <br /> <br /> - It may amuse you to know that one tends to imagine Germaine as played by a younger Mr John Malkovich (To help make him just that little bit shifty and reptilian): also that one imagines his American English as only very rarely accented (Usually when he\u2019s making a point, most especially when needling an \u2018Anglo Saxon\u2019 like Jack).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Also, there just HAS to be Story behind that extensive tattooing: the long hair and short beard can be explained by a Seventeenth century fugitive unable to maintain a clean shave, but those tattoos are clearly much later creations: I wonder if Germaine picked them up with the Anarchs or the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> <br /> - Incidentally, given his character profile describes him as a Fantuc within, a Visionary without, one tends to imagine Germaine as a very vivid conversationalist, but almost completely lacking a sense of humour and/or whimsy (Which doubtless complicates his relations with Smiling Jack \u2026 and everyone else who can crack a smile).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Also, given that Louis Fortier is a younger son of the French aristocracy (Several of whose relatives were obliged to flee La Belle France by The Revolution) and that Monsieur Fortier maintains a quite-literally Baronial style in the LA hills, I\u2019d bet cash money Germaine (Whom one imagines as the epitome of a \u201csea-green incorruptible\u201d) would hate the man and everything he stands for (Not least a relic of the old regime who survived and prospered in the Free States).<br /> <br /> It would not surprise me if Germaine called for Fortier to be purged, that the Baron of West LA was more than willing to defend himself and that it took an intervention (Possibly even an actual show of force) by Jeremy MacNeil to quash this brewing blood feud.<br /> <br /> My mental image is that these two still loathe each other exactly as much as they adore being able to bandy words in the language of home (Bonus points if they\u2019re actually from the same region of France, but very different worlds).<br /> <br /> <br /> - On the other hand the mental image of the painfully patrician Vignes getting on bizarrely well with the formerly-bourgeois Germaine is too delightful to pass up: one assumes that they\u2019re exactly the sort of snobs Germaine built his career on manipulating and that he appreciates their company in the same way that a heavyweight boxer appreciates having a sparring partner to knock around with.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if Germaine is a little bit in denial about missing the sort of \u2018Old World\u2019 civility the Vignes m\u00e9nage abounds in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-10T19:11:06-08:00","id":1548385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548367#post1548367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there just HAS to be Story behind that extensive tattooing: the long hair and short beard can be explained by a Seventeenth century fugitive unable to maintain a clean shave, but those tattoos are clearly much later creations: I wonder if Germaine picked them up with the Anarchs or the Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we go with the rules as written, he shouldn't have any tattoos that postdate his embrace except with something like Vicissitude, but I don't think the writer took that into account. Tattoos are also a terrible way to go incognito which a man on the constant run would want. &quot;Salvador Dali tattoo on the right bicep&quot; would be an easy way to identify him anytime he shows up.<br /> <br /> So I am inclined to ignore that detail and have him be without tattoos, or possibly explain it as some kind of minor magic that perhaps changes what tattoos appear on his upper body at different time periods. Attributing it to Vicissitude would just be boring to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548367#post1548367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, given his character profile describes him as a Fantuc within, a Visionary without, one tends to imagine Germaine as a very vivid conversationalist, but almost completely lacking a sense of humour and/or whimsy (Which doubtless complicates his relations with Smiling Jack \u2026 and everyone else who can crack a smile).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a plausible default personality. It fits his quote of &quot;If I cared what you thought, I'd have asked you, asshole.&quot; The roleplaying hints state he enjoys being belligerent and will purposefully misinterpret innocent statements as hostile just because he loves to argue. He may be charismatic, but he's jvery disagreeable.<br /> <br /> He has some interesting social abilities in his canonical write up. Fast Talking 7. Carousing 5. Etiquette 5. Debate 3. Diplomacy 2. Public Speaking 1. Poetic Expression 1. He's a bull shitter and party goer primarily. Decent debate skills, but has far lower &quot;politician&quot; skills than what we might expect. He is not the guy who riles up the crowd at all, but probably excels in one to one conversations and small soirees where his &quot;charming bully&quot; spiel can &quot;win&quot; arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548367#post1548367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, given that Louis Fortier is a younger son of the French aristocracy (Several of whose relatives were obliged to flee La Belle France by The Revolution) and that Monsieur Fortier maintains a quite-literally Baronial style in the LA hills, I\u2019d bet cash money Germaine (Whom one imagines as the epitome of a \u201csea-green incorruptible\u201d) would hate the man and everything he stands for (Not least a relic of the old regime who survived and prospered in the Free States).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely possible he doesn't like Fortier. Most anarchs in the Free States don't. However, I still see Germaine as someone who does like the good things in life, so he might enjoy Fortier's hospitality even if he trashes the man behind his back. I just imagine most French exiled form home like being in the presence of someone who can bring it back for them.<br /> <br /> While I don't go by canon mechanics anymore (as they often don't make sense), I do use them for some inspiration. While Germaine has some potent stats (likely being from the blood of Critias), Fortier actually has far better abilities in Intimidation, Melee, and Firearms. Germaine actually isn't that much of a fighter, and Fortier is a trained soldier. Without the Brujah Celerity, Fortier would make mince meant out of him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548367#post1548367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand the mental image of the painfully patrician Vignes getting on bizarrely well with the formerly-bourgeois Germaine is too delightful to pass up: one assumes that they\u2019re exactly the sort of snobs Germaine built his career on manipulating and that he appreciates their company in the same way that a heavyweight boxer appreciates having a sparring partner to knock around with.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if Germaine is a little bit in denial about missing the sort of \u2018Old World\u2019 civility the Vignes m\u00e9nage abounds in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think as a duo, Edward and Vera Vignes have more going for them as hosts than by themselves. Both have Etiquette 4, and both have high Music (Edward with 3 and Vera with 4!). So I imagine the couple can be delightful while entertaining guests assuming they appreciate the kind of hospitality such people would provide. Edward also has very high Intimidation (4), and both of them are skilled liars (Subterfuge 4). While LABN characters don't use the Secondary Abilities we see in KMW, I assume Edward's Politics and Law 3 abilities indicate he's a skilled debater and persuader. I'm sure Germaine would argue just as much with them as with anyone else, but he probably enjoys arguing with them more than he does with most anarchs because they're idiots and the Vignes are not. (I imagine he is just as much as a snob even though he also hangs out with the slobs.) He may not appreciate that he cannot win over the Vignes with his standard bullying tactics, but he also knows it is immaterial. These two are never going to try to oppose him physically so he doesn't mind not winning them over. So as you said, they are good sparring partners - in French no less.<br /> <br /> The high level of Music ability for the Vignes is interesting as is Vera having Acting 2 (which I think became Expression in Revised onwards). This is a talented woman, and Edward is no slouch either. I imagine the two of them often played string instruments together. Probably violin duets, but Vera probably plays multiple instruments well. This is probably an artifact of their mortal lives, and it is interesting to build upon things like this when trying to fill in their backstory.<br /> <br /> Fortier and his two childer also have Music, but only at 2. Still, I want to imagine these five holding somewhat regular concertos and other performances. Vera being the soloist, and Edward perhaps filling in on one of the non-stringed instruments if needed. There is no reason why the Free States can't have some class. <br /> <br /> Catherine Dubois's profile says Linguistics 1 (English) so I assume she must be French. Elena also says Linguistics 1 (English), but we know she is Spanish which is mutually intelligible. I imagine living with Louis she's picked up some actual French even if it is not shown on her profile. We don't know much about Mariel St John (who has no Music), but she has Linguistics 2 so I imagine she knows French as well (almost a certainty as a historian of the French &amp; Indian Wars). So there's no reason why the Vignes brood (even their butler Henry Vignes has Linguistics 1) and Fortier and his brides can't spend an entire evening talking French and playing music from time to time. It's enough that Germaine may even bother wearing a shirt for it.<br /> <br /> Interesting, both Jeremy MacNeil and Crispus Attucks have Linguistics 3 as well. Chances are very high they both know French and Spanish as well as another language, as yet unknown. So perhaps even Jeremy might attend these parties. (Smiling Jack is even more polyglot with Linguistics 4 which makes sense given his pirate background. He almost certainly knows French, but I can't imagine him even appearing at a party hosted by Fortier or Edward.) All four of the Brujah Idealists &quot;studying&quot; the Free States have high Linguistics, and they probably all know French. Plus both Professor Habersohn and Countess Andrea Visconti have Music 4. So they might attend these parties as well with another two playing alongside the others.<br /> <br /> If you are going to have all these people know Music, it should show up in game in some way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T12:47:15-08:00","id":1548406,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I\u2019m planning to post a more detailed response to your own reply, but your mental image of a \u2018Kindred classical night\u2019 could only <i>maybe</i> be improved by Smiling Jack showing up with Bela (alias \u2018Hollywood Dracula\u2019 aka \u2018The Anarch Emperor Norton\u2019 and \u2018Da Reel Prince of El-Eh!\u201d in tow.<br /> <br /> Much to the former\u2019s disappointment, the latter is absolutely in his element, completely non-disruptive and actively makes a positive contribution to the event (\u2018Etiquette 4, Performance 4 Acting, Music\u2019 Jack!).<br /> <br /> Nobody is sure they want him back, but everybody dines out on this particular story for years to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-11T16:04:11-08:00","id":1548409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548406#post1548406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I\u2019m planning to post a more detailed response to your own reply, but your mental image of a \u2018Kindred classical night\u2019 could only <i>maybe</i> be improved by Smiling Jack showing up with Bela (alias \u2018Hollywood Dracula\u2019 aka \u2018The Anarch Emperor Norton\u2019 and \u2018Da Reel Prince of El-Eh!\u201d in tow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do intend to make use of Bela in an Emperor Norton type role. He's not going to show up often, but the local Kindred do treat him like a beloved mascot. I'm going with the idea that as &quot;King of the Vampires&quot;, he's quite upset at this upstart Camarilla trying to take over his role. So at the first Rant the PCs attend, at some point there's a dramatic pause as Bela walks in with amused applause, he assumes the stage in hushed silence, and he explains how he pleased he is that his &quot;children&quot; are loyal to him and reject the Camarilla. He then leaves to wild applause.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I have no plans for him to make further appearances unless I think of an appropriate opportunity as things come up. He's very much a one note character, but appropriate as a kind of local flavor. Not much to do with the Free States as a concept, but very much part of LA.<br /> <br /> I want to make him as much of a gentle soul as possible so I'm still thinking of the general way Bela must feed and keep it downlow enough that it does not present Masquerade issues. On the rare occasions he has clarity, I'll be going with Martin Landau's performance in Ed Wood.<br /> <br /> At some point, I do want him and Karen Anotos (from Gangrel Clanbook) to get together in a Mark of the Vampire way as Count Mora and Luna, since Karen is basically Vampira. (I know this character was updated as Lily Thorn in Dread Names, Red List, but I am going to ignore it as the authors clearly disregarded the original intent of GCB - and couldn't even spell the last name right).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T03:35:35-08:00","id":1548424,"title":"","content":"A friend and one correspondent of mine once suggested that Bela putting together (Or quite possibly acquiring through no deliberate effort of his own, but by virtue of what he gets away with) a coterie of Classic Hollywood Vampires - or rather, of Kindred who enjoy messing around in the guise of same, for fun and profit - could potentially be a gaming session (possibly even a campaign) in it\u2019s own right.<br /> <br /> Assuming this game/campaign shows \u2018Our Heroes\u2019 doing their best to take care of \u2018Bela\u2019 whilst the showboating old monomaniac goes about his nightly business - implicitly explaining how somebody who acts and looks <i>exactly</i> like Classic Movie Dracula manages to avoid blowing the Masquerade sky-high - one imagines there could be a truly delightful amount of WHAT WE DO IN THE SHADOWS type antics to play out (Especially with the keen awareness that a deadly serious World of Darkness is waiting to fall on them with a hundred talons and a thousand fangs to lend an edge to the comedy).<br /> <br /> <br /> I remember suggesting that the coterie might include (In addition to Bela as Classic Movie Dracula, Karen Anotos as Vampira - heck, throw in Lily Thorn and let\u2019s see how these two sisters from another mister get along!):-<br /> <br /> - A Tzimisce <i>antitribu</i> as Graf Orlock (At least one actual Nosferatu auditioned, but simply didn\u2019t enjoy being stared at)<br /> <br /> - A rapidly rotating succession of Brujah dudes usually cast as one or more of THE LOST BOYS (There should be a running joke that most of them just walk up in their own street clothes and suit the role perfectly).<br /> <br /> Those willing to put a little more effort in tend to show up as Angel, Spike or suchlike.<br /> <br /> <br /> - A classically-trained thespian who gets really, really into his character\u2019s motivation and fidelity to the literary original in the poshest way possible: this causes a certain amount of comedy when he\u2019s persuaded to play Blade and abject terror when he feels compelled to point out that Bela is getting Dracula <i>wrong</i> (He has showed up as \u2018Count Dracula\u2019 - complete with Moustache - at least once and actual bloodshed was only averted by some sensible person loudly admiring his \u2018Prince Mamwualde\u2019).<br /> <br /> (Yes, he looks exactly like Wesley Snipes but dresses like TOMB OF DRACULA Blade, not the cinematic version, that\u2019s part of the joke).<br /> <br /> <br /> - At least one Ventrue letting his hair down as an Anne Rice vampire<br /> <br /> - At least one Toreador playing somebody like Selene from UNDERWORLD or Alucard from CASTLEVANIA (Since they mostly ARE Anne Rice vampires they have no particular reason to cosplay as same): almost certainly the one who helps run up the costumes<br /> <br /> - One slightly confused City Gangrel wondering if being cast in the role of FROM DUSK \u2018TIL DAWN Snake Vampire is a compliment or an insult (Bonus points if this is Ramona and she\u2019s trying to embody Salma freakin\u2019 Hayek, despite being a scruffy runaway rather than a Romantic poet\u2019s naughty daydream IN SPANISH).<br /> <br /> <br /> Note that not all these characters will be part of the \u2018troupe\u2019 at the same time (One assumes that keeping an eye on/looking out for Bela is one of the few forms of Public Service the Anarchs are willing to accept - but that Bela being a \u2018Deviabt\u2019 by nature, it\u2019s a sufficiently tricky job that it\u2019s quite often employed as a form of community service).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T03:55:27-08:00","id":1548425,"title":"","content":"On a slightly more serious note:-<br /> <br /> (A) I\u2019ve always assumed that it\u2019s practically mandatory (and certainly a Point of local pride) for LA Anarchs to introduce \u2018Bela\u2019 as \u201cThe REAL Prince of LA!\u201d<br /> <br /> Hollywood Dracula usually responds \u201cPRINCE OF <b>DARKNESS</b>\u201d with towering seriousness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Incidentally, I\u2019ve been meaning to ask: do you intend to incorporate characters and elements from VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE - BLOODLINES into your Los Angeles? (That little joke about \u2018Bela\u2019 being the Real Prince of LA and the notion of his being kept an eye on by a coterie occurred to me in the context of Los Angeles under Prince LaCroix).<br /> <br /> <br /> </i>(B) One also assumes that Bela exists mostly to show up when somebody launches into one of those rather shabby \u201cThis ain\u2019t like the movies!\u201d monologues a certain sort of Vampire Movie insists on laying on, apparently to Big themselves up by demeaning the Classics.<br /> <br /> Also as a regular source of \u201cWhat a character! What a city!\u201d anecdotes.<br /> <br /> <br /> (C) As noted above, given Bela\u2019s nature is described as \u2018Deviant\u2019 - and based on the actual Mr Lugosi\u2019s recorded remarks about how excited the female fans got when it came to Classic Movie/Theatre Dracula - while we cannot be entirely certain how Hollywood Dracula goes about his nightly feeding routine, some serious kink is <i>definitely</i> involved (I\u2019m not saying he effectively makes his living as a Vampire Gigolo, but he absolutely could be doing so).<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I tend to assume that \u2018Bela\u2019 was an imitator who showed up to pay his respects on hearing of the death of the historic Mr Lugosi, only to be embraced by the wonderfully-named \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 (A tenth generation Malkavian of possibly-Hungarian origin who seems to have rushed over hoping to preserve his dying idol, then embraced somebody who looked very, very like him* instead).<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Actually, now that I think of it \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 sounds like the sort of eccentric who might deserve a character write-up in his own right: I wonder if he was a rather shy Malkavian who came<br /> out of his shell after seeing a rather younger Bela Lugosi in the DRACULA stage play?<br /> <br /> *<i>In fact I definitely love the idea that \u2018Bela\u2019 looks quite a lot like Mr Martin Landau, as a nod to him not actually being THE Bela Lugosi.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T03:57:11-08:00","id":1548426,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I learned only just today that Mr Bela Lugosi was nearing fifty when he made DRACULA (1931): no wonder they cast him as a vampire, he looked closer to thirty-something!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-12T04:31:47-08:00","id":1548429,"title":"","content":"Forgot to add - assuming the Brujah Idealists Habersohn, Hamilton, Sharaiwa and Visconti are still in LA, I\u2019d bet that Germaine would be quite delighted to drop in for some think-tanking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T06:46:48-08:00","id":1548494,"title":"","content":"Somewhat-belatedly, but as promised, my response to your own thoughts:-<br /> <br /> (1) I tend to see these little contradictions as an excuse to tell an interesting story that explains them and gives some insights into the character - for example, <i>bourgeois</i> to <i>petite-bourgeois</i> Germaine might have adopted them as protective colouring in the distinctly Nineties atmosphere of Anarch LA (Incidentally, I wonder if transfers would vanish from vampiric flesh the way actual tattoos do?).<br /> <br /> These tattoos might have been inflicted on him by an opponent seeking to make it much harder for such a slippery agent to conceal himself and Germaine may be exploiting them in the short term whilst looking for a way to remove them.<br /> <br /> A more subtle variation on the previous point is that they represent a formal covenant (A symbolic way for the character to \u2018burn his bridges\u2019 and acquire further admiration in certain circles), whether as part of a shift in his long-term plans or simply as an expedient.<br /> <br /> Or he might simply have lost a bet with Smiling Jack.<br /> <br /> <br /> (2) Germain definitely has some \u2018Chief of the Secret Police\u2019 vibes, rather than \u2018Fearless Leader\u2019 energy: one suspects that his place on the Red List isn\u2019t the only reason he\u2019s in no real danger of becoming head of the Anarch movement - though one could imagine a scenario where he sneaks and wheedles his way into power DEATH OF STALIN style.<br /> <br /> <br /> (3) It amuses me to imagine Germaine deliberately going Full Revolutionary when holding a conversation (Such polite conversation!) with Baron Fortier in French, with particular emphasis on addressing him as \u2018Citizen\u2019 and using the Revolutionary calendar when giving dates (Something he never bothers with otherwise), whilst Fortier retaliates in kind (For example by giving dates as \u2018In the Year of Our Lord **** on the feast of Saint such-and-such\u2019, also by placing emphasis on <i>Ancien Regime</i> etiquette and titles when mentioning various persons).<br /> <br /> Bonus points if they\u2019re doing all this covert linguistic sniping in the EXACT SAME ACCENT (I really do like the mental image that they\u2019re from the same region of France, albeit from different generations - Fortier being the older - and different social classes).<br /> <br /> Anyway, your description of their distinct capabilities<br /> makes me suspect these two would make a very dangerous combination, if only they didn\u2019t love to loathe each other.<br /> <br /> <br /> (4) I\u2019m not going to lie, the mental image of the deeply-snobbish Vignes keeping themselves afloat in the Anarch Free States mostly because they throw the best concert parties is a thought to treasure (Though I wonder if some of the more thoughtful Anarchs regard them as a useful \u2018miner\u2019s canary\u2019 in terms of ascertaining how local Kindred with natural inclinations towards the Camarilla way of doing things feel about current developments in the Free States).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also deeply amused by the notion of Mr Vignes perpetually lawyering his way out of the trouble his Grumpy Old Snob tendencies get him into on those occasions when he attends a Rant (I sometimes wonder if a key reason the Vignes m\u00e9nage, with all it\u2019s potentially volatile elements, held together for so long is that each of it\u2019s members were terrified by the thought of going their separate ways in the Anarch Free States).<br /> <br /> I wonder if Idiot Fail Childe (but still a Toreador) Christopher ever listens in on these concert parties? He seems to have some unstated, but oddly-close tie to the Vignes (Possibly because he likes the idea of being the young tearaway in this family dynamic, whether the Vignes household like it or not) and their tendency to celebrate the finer things in life may be a key part of their appeal.<br /> <br /> - I would suggest making Catherine Dubois specifically a <i>colonial</i> Frenchwoman (Born overseas in some French holding, possibly in Guadeloupe) to help explain what drew Fortier to her specifically - her family is very much the sort of person he himself was in his breathing days.<br /> <br /> - I\u2019d bet Germaine would wear a shirt AND a cravat with ladies present and Higher Culture in the air (Not a tie though, that would just be selling out).<br /> <br /> - One imagines that Elena can understand enough French to know when to smile and nod, as well as take simple instructions (But that her eyes tend to glaze over a bit when things get more complicated).<br /> <br /> - Given that Jeremy MacNeil hails from a highland clan of the 1600s, it\u2019s possible that one of those Linguistics dots is for English, given that his native language would almost certainly be Scots Gaelic (In fact I\u2019d bet that \u2018Jeremy\u2019 is an anglicisation of his birth name).<br /> <br /> - It amuses me to imagine Jeremy MacNeil carefully avoiding the Vignes gatherings as a rule (Partly because they\u2019re expert snobs, partly because Mrs Vignes kept giving him excessively familiar looks and he Does Not Want that sort of Drama), but Crispus Attucks being a semi-regular guest (Partly because, as suggested above, the Vignes make an excellent \u2018test audience\u2019 for non-Anarch reactions, party because he misses New England - and the Vignes are New England to the Bone - partly because the Vignes are always deeply, deeply happy to demonstrate their Abolitionist credentials with such a <i>nice</i> Negro Gentleman - a Revolutionary War hero too!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T11:24:45-08:00","id":1548496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548494#post1548494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Germain definitely has some \u2018Chief of the Secret Police\u2019 vibes, rather than \u2018Fearless Leader\u2019 energy: one suspects that his place on the Red List isn\u2019t the only reason he\u2019s in no real danger of becoming head of the Anarch movement - though one could imagine a scenario where he sneaks and wheedles his way into power DEATH OF STALIN style.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn't be a bad gimmick for the character. One of the &quot;services&quot; he often provides is identifying and exposing the rats and informants among the local anarch groups he visits. He doesn't do it in LA because no one likes people who do that kind of thing and he needs to keep coming back there, but it's OK to do it once in a city he visits and may not show up again for several decades if ever. He's definitely prone to conspiracy himself so he understands that kind of life, and he probably has a long lifetime experience of dealing with cells being exposed. So with that kind of experience, he just has a feel for this and recognizes little signs of suspicion that he follows up on. <br /> <br /> He doesn't show up to do that. He just wants another place to hide for a while, gets involved in the local anarchs, helps them out in some matter or another, and if he happens to ferret out a snitch at the same time, so be it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548494#post1548494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m also deeply amused by the notion of Mr Vignes perpetually lawyering his way out of the trouble his Grumpy Old Snob tendencies get him into on those occasions when he attends a Rant (I sometimes wonder if a key reason the Vignes m\u00e9nage, with all it\u2019s potentially volatile elements, held together for so long is that each of it\u2019s members were terrified by the thought of going their separate ways in the Anarch Free States).</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine Edward Vignes attends Rants simply to keep apprised as to what's happening so he's not caught off guard and to show everyone else that he's &quot;loyal&quot;. He doesn't speak up unless some issue directly affects his concerns in Pasadena. After being burned back in Boston and seeing what happened to Don Sebastian and the others in 1944, I imagine he just wants to be left alone. He'll work with whoever is in charge. He'd be more than happy to live under a Prince loyal to the Camarilla, but would not bother to help the Camarilla establish themselves. The only time he'd actually fight is against someone like the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> As written, Edward is simply the &quot;baron&quot; of Pasadena with his brood the only vampires there. He's not interested in power or ambition. He just wants to live alone and not be troubled. I imagine he's similar in certain ways to the master vampire of The Lost Boys played by Edward Herrmann. In my version of the Free States, he watches over the other &quot;outlands&quot; of the San Gabriel Valley and San Rafael Hills (basically his brood and the Blount sisters plus perhaps 1-2 more who fit in with them). Edward and the others are officially under the &quot;protection&quot; of Louis Fortier, but de facto Edward is in charge. I dislike the idea that &quot;barons&quot; are just whoever is in charge of any little area, so it is an easy way to increase the territory under Fortier's control and cement his status more. His own personal power, support from the other local vampires, the protection of Fortier, and that he doesn't try to lead anything is enough that the younger vampires leave him alone.<br /> <br /> Plus the somewhat friendship of Crispus Attucks from their old days back in Boston. I like the idea that Crispus may informally talk to Vignes to get his opinion so he understands how an outsider may interpret things. Edward would be willing to reveal things to Crispus in these informal meetings that he would never ever say at a Rant since he knows Crispus will keep it confidential. Entertaining a noted personality of the War of Independence would appeal to the Vignes, and I had not thought of that before. And both Edward and Vera probably do like the visits of that nice Negro Gentleman in an honest, and only slightly condescending way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T13:44:59-08:00","id":1548570,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not going to lie, Mr Edward Hermann would be PERFECT for the role (Also, given then Anarchs aren\u2019t the most meticulous sorts it makes perfect sense that their use of \u2018Baron\u2019 is deeply casual and based on a definition more intuitive than systematic).<br /> <br /> On a related note, may I ask if any of the Ventrue from LA BY NIGHT have canonical \u2018bloody types\u2019 associated with their Clan Weakness? (Given that a Ventrue\u2019s feeding preferences are as - or should be as - revealing as their sexual preferences, it\u2019s not wholly unreasonable to leave that sort of thing to the judgement of the individual storyteller, but the Clan Weakness of the Ventrue fascinates me and I\u2019ve had a few ideas of my own for various characters).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, where would be the best place to post ideas for the characterisation of individuals like Maria of San Diego or Nicholas of the Second LA Setite temple?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-18T18:14:27-08:00","id":1548577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548570#post1548570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a related note, may I ask if any of the Ventrue from LA BY NIGHT have canonical \u2018bloody types\u2019 associated with their Clan Weakness? (Given that a Ventrue\u2019s feeding preferences are as - or should be as - revealing as their sexual preferences, it\u2019s not wholly unreasonable to leave that sort of thing to the judgement of the individual storyteller, but the Clan Weakness of the Ventrue fascinates me and I\u2019ve had a few ideas of my own for various characters).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, their descriptions do not go into that which is one of many weaknesses of the sourcebook. There are nine Ventrue with character write ups in that sourcebook, and none of them are given that critical information. It makes sense to give Louis Fortier the stereotypical restriction of only feeding on members of the opposite sex, but the others don't have such obvious directions. I am tempted to keep that as a theme for Fortier's own childer/brides and do some variation of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1548570#post1548570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, where would be the best place to post ideas for the characterisation of individuals like Maria of San Diego or Nicholas of the Second LA Setite temple?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just created another thread where you can comment on any canon NPCs or groups in LA that people want.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T13:39:21-08:00","id":1548596,"title":"","content":"Thank You most kindly! (I shall post something there presently, hopefully today and most definitely tomorrow).<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, their descriptions do not go into that which is one of many weaknesses of the sourcebook. There are nine Ventrue with character write ups in that sourcebook, and none of them are given that critical information. It makes sense to give Louis Fortier the stereotypical restriction of only feeding on members of the opposite sex, but the others don't have such obvious directions. I am tempted to keep that as a theme for Fortier's own childer/brides and do some variation of them. </div> </div> </div><br /> I\u2019ll post my more detailed thoughts on those other Ventrue in the new thread, but since you bring this up here one would like to say that - were I a GM - \u201cMembers of the opposite sex\u201d would be far too generic to be accepted as a \u2018Blood Type\u2019 (Even for an NPC - perhaps especially for a powerful NPC, since players will likely need all the help and hooks they can get when dealing with the likes of \u2018Baron\u2019 Fortier).<br /> <br /> For my money something that leans more into the complex mixture of fear, mystery and gratitude that Louis Fortier must feel towards his enigmatic sire \u2018Night Star\u2019 would make a better inspiration for his preferred Blood Type (Perhaps \u2018Lady of the Night\u2019 \u2018La Belle Canadienne\u2019, \u2018Mystery Woman\u2019 or \u2018Colonial Belle\u2019 might evoke a more specific archetype from which to build out Louis Fortier\u2019s feeding restriction), not least because there would be elements of \u2018Foreign Culture Fetish\u2019 and vaguely Oedipal overtones that lend a suitably psychosexual edge to the Clan Weakness.<br /> <br /> In any case, one of my rules for coming up with a Ventrue\u2019s \u2018blood type\u2019 is that it should boil down to a descriptive archetype (\u2018Wild Colonial\u2019 \u2018Valkyrie\u2019 \u2018Soldier Boy\u2019 \u2018\u2019Rough Trade\u2019 and so on): as a preview of forthcoming attractions, my personal pick for the Vigne\u2019s blood type would definitely be \u2018Couple Goals\u2019 (Although that\u2019s not a term either husband or wife is likely to use, it does vividly illustrate a tendency to target happy couples, likely grounded in their own much-soured attitude to marriage and to each other).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-19T18:52:12-07:00","id":1549454,"title":"","content":"Since I want to make Germaine a prominent character in the chronicle, I should also include Countess D\u2019Adhemar in some way. Her desire to destroy Germaine and his inclusion on the Red List are essential to any story that includes him. She could also serve as a good antagonist in general. Of course, we know very little about the Countess or her quest so once again STs need to do some heavy lifting here.<br /> <br /> First, we need a new name for her. Countess D\u2019Adhemar is probably her mortal name, but it shouldn\u2019t be how she is known currently in vampire society. There probably lots of other Kindred who were once countesses, and her family name or title doesn\u2019t work for me. While I could give her a random French feminine name, I\u2019ll use something based on Adhemar. That is based on a masculine Germanic name, and it had a feminine form of Adamardis which was later reduced to Aenor which was later replaced in turn by Eleanor (at least according to Wikipedia) so that is what I am going with. Or perhaps a variant like Leonora or Nora.<br /> <br /> Second, I\u2019ll be placing Eleanor in San Francisco. It\u2019s the closest Camarilla stronghold to the Free States and gives her some opportunity to observe Germaine's comings and goings to Los Angeles. Germaine travels a lot, but Eleanor herself needs some kind of base somewhere and San Francisco makes sense. It also makes it easier for PCs to somehow encounter her if they ever visit San Francisco (or possibly even to confront and attempt to destroy her.) An appearance at the Vampire Club is probably essential if the PCs ever visit that. Germaine may not be aware there is any \u201cEleanor\u201d in San Francisco, and even if he\u2019s heard the name does not know she is Countess D\u2019Adhemar.<br /> <br /> Third, we need some backstory for her after 1793. Eleanor is likely known as a prominent French Toreador and childe of Madame Guil (though one she has cut off), but her involvement with Germaine and French Revolution are unknown. She should have her own reputation she\u2019s established in the past two hundred years while she\u2019s been secretly seeking Germaine\u2019s destruction. She likely pursued him to North America fairly early though not immediately given her commitments in Paris. Let\u2019s say after Napoleon\u2019s downfall when it became safe again to travel between France and the United States. That gives Germaine at least a twenty year head start. Maybe she entered through Boston (like Annabelle Triabel did) or New Orleans, a domain with close links to France.<br /> <br /> Since we\u2019ve assigned Germaine some activities in Mexico, it would make sense for her to have spent some time in the Camarilla domain of Veracruz. Maybe even arriving there first during the first French Intervention in 1838. Perhaps she even met Lodin while he was there (1847-1869 or so) which covers not only the Mexican-American War, but the Reform War and Second French Intervention. This tulmutuous time would be good cover for Anarch activities in Mexico. Then after Germaine left, her going to New Orleans as a base would be convenient. Then at some point after the Free States were created she might choose San Francisco thinking Germaine would make use of that.<br /> <br /> Fourth, what should be her general abilities? She must have skills in political manipulation and treachery, but she was also a skilled enough fighter to almost kill Germaine back in 1793 and did destroy numerous ghouls of Critias who attempted to defend him. As Madame Guil\u2019s childe, she is of the seventh generation just one less than Germaine, and is slightly older than him. Overall, she should be an equal opponent although probably less skilled in combat, but more skilled socially.<br /> <br /> She should have some agents and spies in Los Angeles. Probably mortals and ghouls, but she may have one or a few Kindred informants. Perhaps she\u2019s seduced or even blood bonded some anarch Kindred who visited San Francisco or got close to the border in San Jose. (I need to start a new thread on the Camarilla\u2019s agents within the Free States since it is large enough for its own topic, and I\u2019ll be sure to mention the Countess there as well.) Germaine keeps himself isolated from most Kindred (although we\u2019ve built some ideas here on who he might associate himself with when he\u2019s in LA) so the chances these spies ever ingratiate themselves with Germaine is slim. However, they should a description and know what to look for even if they don\u2019t know it is \u201cGermaine of the Red List\u201d they are looking for. So the PCs might witness someone observing Germaine at some and investigate. Perhaps this is even what begins the process of them figuring out who he actually is. Another possibility is for the PCs not to realize it is Germaine being observed because they witness this at some event where other Kindred are in attendance like a music salon hosted by Fortier with guests like the Vignes couple, the Brujah Idealists,<br /> <br /> I think any attempt to destroy Germaine in Los Angeles itself is a fool\u2019s errand. Too many things are stacked against that. So any assassination attempt would likely happen when Germaine leaves to enter a Camarilla domain. For story purposes then, the PCs would need to discover someone trying to determine Germaine\u2019s future itinerary and destination. That still means she needs some other combat oriented Kindred to accompany her when the final hit goes down.<br /> <br /> Fifth, their previous relationship as lovers during the French Revolution can provide us some good character movements. Though their relationship was mainly about exploiting one another for their own secret ends, it is stated she was enamored by his handsome face and impertinent manner. More of a plaything than than a boyfriend, but that doesn\u2019t mean there wasn\u2019t real sparks during their lovemaking. There might not be a personal attachment and it\u2019s likely the two have never seen each other since 1793, but there should be some chemistry besides the hate. When the truth comes out, I\u2019d want the PCs to see some kind of personal reaction rather than if some unrelated Kindred was trying to kill Germaine.<br /> <br /> Ideas and thoughts on Countess D'Adhemar are appreciated. She has the potential to be an important antagonist in the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T13:54:51-07:00","id":1549464,"title":"","content":"I think we can all agree that the sensible question when it comes to <i>la Comtesse d\u2019Adhemar</i> is \u201cWe all know that she and Germain are DANGEROUS LIASONS, all the time, but are talking Glenn Close &amp; John Malkovich, Lindsey Duncan &amp; Alan Rickman or Annette Bening &amp; Colin Firth?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Some slightly more serious thoughts, in brief:-<br /> <br /> - I\u2019m assuming that the lady was born somewhere in the late 1740s/early 1750s AD (Making her a contemporary of Favourites like Lamballe or Polignac, who had the ear of Marie Antoinette): it\u2019s possible her sire \u2018Gilles\u2019 (Presumably Madam Guil often employed a male guise during her days as an Anarch, prior to the French Revolution) Embraced her as much because the Countess was getting \u201ctoo long in the tooth\u201d as to reward her for getting close to the Royal Court<br /> <br /> <br /> - From what I can tell, \u2018Eleanor\u2019 (or \u2018Eleanore\u2019 in French usage) wasn\u2019t really popular in the French Aristocracy of the 18th century: all the Eleanor\u2019s of that era which I\u2019ve been able to trace are English or Germanic or even Swedish<br /> <br /> My own inclination wouod be to make her birth name \u2018Marie Joseph\u2019 and show this an attempt to curry favour with Maria Josepha, who married the father of Louis XVI in AD 1747 (Suggesting the future Countess could have been born in that year).<br /> <br /> <br /> - I wonder if making her a native of Lorraine (The ancestral homeland of Marie Antoinette\u2019s father, acquired from Austria by France and a subject of possessive interest to the Imperial family as a result) would help explain how she caught the Queen\u2019s interest<br /> <br /> <br /> - I\u2019m also tempted to suggest that the Countess was specifically tied to the Orleanist party at court (Since that was a faction of the Royal family that seems to have pursued some sort of whispering campaign against Marie Antoinette and would have been quite useful to the future Madame Guil, as she worked to lay out the groundwork for a future Anarch revolt): incidentally, the former Duke of Orelans actually voted for the execution of the King, his cousin, yet his heir Louis-Philippe somehow became King of the French anyway (Despite no fewer than three generation of the Royal families\u2019 senior branch standing in the way).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying it was vampires, but in the World of Darkness it absolutely could have been vampires<br /> <br /> <br /> - Given her title and the Salic nature of French succession laws (Also the obvious opportunity to suggest parallels with Merteuil of DANGEROUS LIASONS) I\u2019m assuming that the Countess married into her peerage and was widowed at a relatively young age<br /> <br /> If you want to run with the name Eleanor/Eleanora as her birth name, you could suggest that she was the daughter of foreign nobles who married into the French aristocracy (Adding another parallel to Marie Antoinette that might breed mutual sympathy).<br /> <br /> Whether she left a line of descendants is an interesting question<br /> <br /> <br /> - I\u2019m assuming the future Madame Guil, then an Anarch (and at one point one of the most notorious diablerists in France) acquired the Countess as a way to put a respectable face on her operations: also, perhaps, as somebody who could tutor her in how to pass in High Society (In addition to acting as her mortal agent)<br /> <br /> Given that the French Revolution was NOT the start of the Second Anarch Revolt, it seems reasonable to deduce that a key part of Kritias\u2019 interest in planting a mole close to the Countess was to ensure that this would be the case (I.E. In order to make sure that the Mortal Revolt would not be accompanied by a Vampiric one)<br /> <br /> <br /> - Finally, at least for now, it\u2019s interesting to wonder if the Countess served as \u2018Madame Guil\u2019s in for the Camarilla: it\u2019s even vaguely possible that she agreed to pose as Sire of the latter to muddy the waters, then required that Germain be put on the Red List as quid pro quo for letting her \u2018Childe\u2019 completely overshadow her for the rest of Camarilla history.<br /> <br /> Whether or not this was the case, one can easily imagine the Countess pursuing Germain as a way to keep a safe distance from her remarkably cruel Sire (Who could well have seen her as a loose end to be tidied away, given her awareness of at least some of Madame Guil\u2019s secret history).<br /> <br /> She might be formally ranked as a subordinate to the Toreador Justicar (If this is the case then Petrodon of Nosferatu is likely to regard her with some small suspicion - given the traditional tensions the clans and the possibility of one Justicar sticking their oar into another\u2019s home waters).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the Countess might well be Madame Guil\u2019s \u2018Anarch Whisperer\u2019 an agent who keeps up relations with the most interesting parties in the Free States (Either through formal or informal channels).<br /> <br /> In any case, it seems highly unlikely that Madam Guil would share her Sabbat connections with her Childe (In fact my previous thoughts on the Countess was that she might know too much for Madam Guil to permit her to exist - taking up her Childe\u2019s feud with Germain as a way of making peace with her memory after \u2018recovering\u2019 her vitae).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T13:55:24-07:00","id":1549465,"title":"","content":"These are just my initial thoughts: there may be more to come tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T21:49:43-07:00","id":1549471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1549464#post1549464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own inclination wouod be to make her birth name \u2018Marie Joseph\u2019 and show this an attempt to curry favour with Maria Josepha, who married the father of Louis XVI in AD 1747 (Suggesting the future Countess could have been born in that year).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1549464#post1549464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to run with the name Eleanor/Eleanora as her birth name, you could suggest that she was the daughter of foreign nobles who married into the French aristocracy (Adding another parallel to Marie Antoinette that might breed mutual sympathy).</div> </div> </div> </div>My intention was to use Eleanor as her pseudonym among vampires, not her given name as a mortal. So your suggestion is fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1549464#post1549464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m assuming the future Madame Guil, then an Anarch (and at one point one of the most notorious diablerists in France) acquired the Countess as a way to put a respectable face on her operations: also, perhaps, as somebody who could tutor her in how to pass in High Society (In addition to acting as her mortal agent)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Countess is described as a Toreador neonate of Madame Guil so it is highly likely all her actions furthering the Revolution was done at her behest. Madame Guil herself would be over two hundred years herself and could have easily manipulated the Countess to do anything. It's a question if the Countess actually realized the extent of her actions, or if her mortal politics mirrored her actions as a vampire. That she was described as a friend of Queen Marie Antoinette leads me to believe as a mortal, she was probably quite in tune with her friend, but the allure of pleasing her sire was more important than any mortal connections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1549464#post1549464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the French Revolution was NOT the start of the Second Anarch Revolt, it seems reasonable to deduce that a key part of Kritias\u2019 interest in planting a mole close to the Countess was to ensure that this would be the case (I.E. In order to make sure that the Mortal Revolt would not be accompanied by a Vampiric one)</div> </div> </div> </div>Critias moved to the New World a little after the execution of Marie Antoinette (in late October 1793), and we know the timing was a result of a summons by his sire, Menele. What Critias' actual intentions were by supporting the revolutionaries is unknown. However, it may be pertinent that his ghouled agents were members of the Girondins, not the Jacobins.<br /> <br /> We know from other sourcebooks that the French Revolution was a hotbead of anarch activity, but they were clearly crushed by the end. In order to provide some backstory to the Phoenix Society, a secret group of anarchs mentioned in New Orleans By Night, I retconned them into being anarchs who did attempt a second Anarch Revolt at that time. The phoenix in their name representing the anarch movement being reborn from the ashes. They have absolutely no idea who the hell this Germaine guy is, or why his name is mentioned as being involved in their activities. They think Germaine must have been doing his own thing at this time, and inadvertently screwed up their plans by his incompetence. So they hate the guy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1549464#post1549464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, at least for now, it\u2019s interesting to wonder if the Countess served as \u2018Madame Guil\u2019s in for the Camarilla: it\u2019s even vaguely possible that she agreed to pose as Sire of the latter to muddy the waters, then required that Germain be put on the Red List as quid pro quo for letting her \u2018Childe\u2019 completely overshadow her for the rest of Camarilla history.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're given almost nothing about the relationship between the Countess and Guil. We just know that Guil is mentioned as having deserted the Countess. I interpret that to mean that Madame Guil purposefully distanced herself from the Countess just in case it ever came up that she was involved in the late unpleasantness at Paris. It's likely Madame Guil put Germaine on the Red List to further distance herself from her childe. Why she hasn't destroyed her childe herself is a bit of a mystery, but it's possible Guil thinks that might be too suspicious, and that the two have an understanding to just forget the whole thing because it could take them both down.<br /> <br /> So I personally am putting their relationship as quite strained, but there's not much she can do to a sire much older than her who is now a Justicar. The Countess's hunt for Germaine is simply to eliminate any potential threat he could prove to her by revealing how much information she gave him that allowed the Brujah to outmaneuver the Toreador.<br /> <br /> Whether or not this was the case, one can easily imagine the Countess pursuing Germain as a way to keep a safe distance from her remarkably cruel Sire (Who could well have seen her as a loose end to be tidied away, given her awareness of at least some of Madame Guil\u2019s secret history).<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that while she is one her own rogue mission to destroy Germaine, that she probably supports Justicar Petrodon in some capacity, but not to the extent it would cause him to question why she wants to help or figure out that she has an interest in Germaine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-21T12:27:33-07:00","id":1549485,"title":"","content":"Regarding your own replies:-<br /> <br /> (1) While I have no particular ancestry picked out for Marie-Josephe, Comtesse d\u2019Adhemar, it did occur to me that making her birthplace Valmont in the Moselle might well be another nice nod to DANGEROUS LIASONS (Alas, I have been unable to locate any place in France called Merteuil), as well as my notion of the Countess hailing from the place where France met the German States.<br /> <br /> <br /> (2) If I remember correctly, there\u2019s at least some evidence for elements within the French court being friendly to the face of Marie Antoinette, but rude (and even treacherous) behind her back; one should also never forget the material advantages of befriending a Queen, especially a queen of France under the Ancient Regime.<br /> <br /> For what it\u2019s worth, I tend to imagine the Countess as a Bon Vivant in demeanour and a Conspirator by nature; with this in mind, one would further imagine that she personally liked Marie Antoinette, but was perfectly prepared to exploit the connection (primarily in order to serve her own interests) and that her price for actively betraying the Queen\u2019s interests was nothing less than the Embrace.<br /> <br /> <br /> (3) My guess is that Critias, whom one imagines as an instinctive Oligarch of the Platonic sort, planted a mole primarily to ensure that the future Madame Guil did not end up holding the reigns of power in France - I may have mentioned previously that one imagines her late, unlamented sire as a sometime headache of the Brujah methuselah and that his hostility towards the Childe may have stemmed from his hostility to her Sire and to her Anarch politics alike.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also possible that she was too much a Medea for Kritias to find the thought of her anywhere near the levers of power at all appealing (One imagines that even at his best Kritias tends to imagine powerful woman as exceptional, rather than exemplary, very much as one would expect of an Ancient Athenian).<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, I like your idea for the Phoenix Society a great deal.<br /> <br /> <br /> (4) I tend to assume that, at least prior to her defection from the Camarilla, Madame Guil was devious enough to appreciate the services of a Childe who knew the secret of her prior career (Though not all her secrets, by any means).<br /> <br /> One further assumes that the Countess quite deliberately made herself both useful and absent - acting as a messenger and emissary plenipotentiary for her Sire, whether or not she was granted any formal title - based on her suspicion that if she ever stops being too useful to get rid of Madame will get rid of her.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, I\u2019d bet she gets sent in where Madame Guil requires a charm offensive.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also think that, given Germain IS on the Red List, The Countess\u2019 mission to destroy him is less a Rogue op and more of an independent endeavour (Not least because Germain works to make himself a destabilising influence in Camarilla domains), at least so long as she avoids risking too much, too blatantly in Anarch territory.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also possible that, if the destruction of an individual on the Red List comes with any sort of reward (I\u2019m not sure if this is actually the case), then the Countess might well be grateful for something that would burnish her prestige and material assets.<br /> <br /> <br /> One final possibility which occurs to me is that the relationship between Germain and the Countess might be depicted as having a deep, though not friendly, mutual connection - based on mutual fascination, a spy\u2019s willingness to intrigue with their opposite numbers and a keen suspicion their own side is as likely to get them killed as their enemies.<br /> <br /> Not really a Love/Hate relationship, more a mutual reluctance to waste a potential Intelligence coup by destroying a rival who could potentially be of use (After all, given that The Countess is certainly afraid of Madame Guil, it\u2019s at least conceivable she might defect to the Anarchs - and who would be better placed than Germain to understand how very, very credible that possibility is?).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-21T12:28:04-07:00","id":1549486,"title":"","content":"So basically DANGEROUS LIASONS by way of John Le Carre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T20:04:06-07:00","id":1549510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1549485#post1549485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s also possible that, if the destruction of an individual on the Red List comes with any sort of reward (I\u2019m not sure if this is actually the case), then the Countess might well be grateful for something that would burnish her prestige and material assets.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kindred Most Wanted sourcebook does go into Trophy clans and what each Trophy can provide the person who slays or brings in one of the Anathema. While it's not clear how it works, from what I can figure out is that each clan of the Camarilla (through their member of the Inner Circle) offers a &quot;trophy&quot; for each member of the Anathema. This gets reevaluated every time the Inner Circle meets, and if the Anathema's trophy is not claimed in the past session, another clan gets the honor of awarding the Trophy and sweetening the offer. (Although this could also be the Justicars inbetween the meetings of the Inner Circle) This isn't always so, as the Anathema in question can be so highly desired by one clan that the clan convinces the others to let it keep being the Trophy clan (Kemintiri for the Ventrue is the best example). Predictably, Germaine's Trophy clan as of 1994 was Toreador (and he might have only been put on there in 1985). (I don't know what the latest sourcebook states his Trophy clan is).<br /> <br /> The sourcebook gives various examples of Trophy boons, but this is an OOC section designed to help STs decide what could be given. I imagine multiple trophy boons can be given, especially for those Anathema who stay on the list for a while. At the lowest end, you can get this like prestige (Status), clan friendship (presumably the Merit), and various benefits one can normally obtain only though the Prince (likely through a domain already ruled by one of that clan). They also get a permanent (magical) tattoo on their hand that marks them as such, and thus presumably proof of their accomplishment. However, this portion of the text doesn't make clear if it is talking only about Alastors (who may or may not have destroyed one of the Anathema) or non-Alastors who did destroy an anathema. A lot of this OOC section in KMW is written like that. It could have been written much clearer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine?p=1549485#post1549485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One final possibility which occurs to me is that the relationship between Germain and the Countess might be depicted as having a deep, though not friendly, mutual connection - based on mutual fascination, a spy\u2019s willingness to intrigue with their opposite numbers and a keen suspicion their own side is as likely to get them killed as their enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem to be the canonical relationship between the characters, but I am applying canon only very loosely here. I'm more concerned about having something gameable for the PCs. I'm not interested in a deadly feud between Countess D'Adhemar and Germaine that cannot involve the PCs in any way or in only a minor way, but something they can experience in a cool way where their decisions matter.<br /> <br /> So I am open to a Valmont/Merteuil style feud between the two. It certainly gives me a notion of how to run Countess D'Adhemar at least (Glenn Close gave an amazing performance in Dangerous Liaisions, and I am familiar enough with it to help me RP the character). But I am not sure how to get the PCs into the middle of that, or how they could interact with it.<br /> <br /> I do have notions of the PCs possibly meeting the Countess (as &quot;Eleanor&quot;) at the Vampire Club in San Francisco should they ever go there, but Germaine will never go there. I could have the Countess already know whatever alias Germaine is using while in LA, so she could speak intelligently to the PCs about him (assuming I succeeded in getting them interested in that PC), sound them out, and if she think it's safe to tip her hand, begin asking them questions or request favors concerning him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 03-24-2025, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-24T09:29:13-07:00","id":1549538,"title":"","content":"I suspect the best way to put PCs in the middle between Madame la Comtesse and Germain would be to have one recruit them as spies, then show the other attempt to recruit them as double agents and then let Our Heroes decide whether to stick with one or the other or so their best to play both for fools \u2026 or run from all this Evil Exes Spy Drama.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this rather assumes that the Countess is Germain\u2019s equal &amp; opposite - somebody seeking to prop up what he seeks to tear down and ground what he desires to see take flight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}